[{"headline":"Merthyr Tydfil projects controllable earmarked reserves down from 15,694 to 9,599 by March 2027","lead":"Merthyr Tydfil council's papers for its Cabinet meeting on 22 October project that its controllable earmarked reserves, money set aside for named purposes, will fall from 15,694 on 31 March 2026 to 9,599 on 31 March 2027. Appendix 3 gives the figures as they appear in its table, without stating a unit in the material the desk reviewed.\n\nThe table shows the drop is steepest in 2026/27. The corporate part of those reserves is projected to fall from 11,674 on 31 March 2026 to 6,077 on 31 March 2027. The controllable total is then projected at 7,671 on 31 March 2028, 7,426 on 31 March 2029 and 7,348 on 31 March 2030.\n\nThe projection ends at 7,216 on 31 March 2031. The decline after March 2028 is much smaller than in the first year of the projection, with the total falling by 455 over the three years from March 2028 to March 2031.","iso":"2026-10-22","paper_title":"Appendix 3","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77199/77199.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-11-25","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Committee Report","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77447/77447.pdf","headline":"Schools received \u00a3860k of additional ALN grant in 2026/27, with no additional efficiency contribution requested from schools in 2025/26 or 2026/27","detail":"The paper says schools face significant pressures from pay, pensions and increased ALN demand. It says that due to the scale of the Council's challenge, protecting schools will remain difficult.","category":"demand","matters":"Schools' ALN demand and the limited protection from further efficiency requests are a common pressure across councils and the detail is useful for comparison.","figures":"\u00a3860k additional ALN grant (2026/27); no efficiency contribution requested in 2025/26 or 2026/27","quote":"During 2026/27 Merthyr Tydfil schools received additional grant funding of \u00a3860k to support ALN costs","read_on":"2026-11-20","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-25","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Committee Report","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77447/77447.pdf","headline":"Fees and charges to rise in line with CPI of 3.5% for the 12 months to September 2026","detail":"Charges are adjusted annually to CPI published the September before the financial year. The increase applies to all charges unless a service provides a robust business case for an alternative.","category":"income","matters":"Peer councils using the same September CPI rule can compare their income uplift assumptions directly.","figures":"3.5% CPI (12 months to September 2026)","quote":"CPI rose by 3.5% in the 12 months to September 2026.","read_on":"2026-11-20","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-25","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Committee Report","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77447/77447.pdf","headline":"Council tax planning assumption of 5% a year maintained, with no decision yet for 2027/28","detail":"The paper says council tax provides just over 20% of the Council Fund funding contribution and that any variation from the 5% planning assumption would change the funding gap. The Council will again aim to restrict any increase to the minimum possible.","category":"income","matters":"The council tax assumption is one of the few levers within a council's control, and the paper signals it may be set lower than planned.","figures":"5% planning assumption per year; just over 20% share of funding; around 77% AEF share","quote":"No decision has yet been determined for 2027/28.","read_on":"2026-11-20","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-25","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Committee Report","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77447/77447.pdf","headline":"Teachers' Pension Scheme employer rate to fall from 28.6% to 17.6% from April 2027, with the Merthyr Tydfil impact not yet validated","detail":"The government has announced the lower employer rate, with funding reduced to match so the change is cost neutral for public sector employers overall. The paper says the impact on Merthyr Tydfil CBC has not been validated.","category":"other","matters":"Every Welsh council employing teachers faces the same rate change, and the offsetting funding adjustment will determine whether it helps the budget gap.","figures":"28.6% (current TPS employer rate); 17.6% (rate from April 2027)","quote":"employer contribution rates for the Teachers\u2019 Pension Scheme (TPS) will decrease from 28.6% to 17.6%.","read_on":"2026-11-20","material":true},{"iso":"2026-11-25","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Committee Report","paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77447/77447.pdf","headline":"Corporate management asked to evaluate what a 5% cost reduction would require in each service area","detail":"The paper says the work is continuing and that identifying areas that will not affect service quality and standards has proven difficult. Options listed include reducing discretionary services and changing the standard or frequency of statutory services.","category":"savings","matters":"Service-by-service 5% reduction exercises show how far councils are going to find savings after years of prior cuts, and what options they are considering.","figures":"5% cost reduction (evaluated for each service area)","quote":"Corporate Management have been challenged to evaluate what a 5% cost reduction would require for each service area.","read_on":"2026-11-20","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-11-17"},"name":"Merthyr Tydfil","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-11-20","since_iso":"2026-10-21","distress":false,"headline":"\u00a3158k Hardship Funding \u2013 Supporting Digital Transformation reserve is proposed to be consolidated into the Transformation Programme Reserve","lead":"Internal borrowing from a transformation reserve for invest-to-save schemes is a method a finance director may want to compare with their own approach to funding transformation.","also":["26 other findings in this window","20 papers caught"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-11-25","n_findings":27,"n_documents":20,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 4","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.merthyr.gov.uk/documents/s77200/77200.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":78,"news_drafts_total":1}}